open MeasureTheory

namespace PhysReaudit

/-- **Validity of the two-sided SPRT** (Q. Li, *When Can Physical Evidence Survive a World-Model Update?*, review revision of 3 November 2026 (sha256 a20c437b…), proof of Theorem 4, p.4 (PDF p.5)): "Thus eSn is a nonnegative
supermartingale, and Ville's inequality bounds false acceptance by δ. … The lower-boundary probability is
at most δ."

Let `0 < q₀ < t < 1`, `0 < δ < 1/2`, `a ∈ (0, 1]`, any depth `d` and any side law `ν`.
1. For every `q ∈ [t, 1]`, under the Bernoulli(q) target tape `e^{S_n}` is a nonnegative supermartingale
   for `F_n = σ(Y_1, …, Y_n)`.
2. For every `q ∈ [t, 1]`, the SPRT accepts with probability at most `δ`.
3. For every `q ∈ [0, q₀]`, the SPRT stops without a certificate (at the lower boundary) with probability
   at most `δ`. -/
theorem sprt_validity {W : Type} [MeasurableSpace W] (ν : Measure W) [IsProbabilityMeasure ν]
    {q₀ t δ a : ℝ} {d : ℕ} (h0 : 0 < q₀) (h1 : q₀ < t) (h2 : t < 1) (hδ : 0 < δ) (hδ1 : δ < 1 / 2)
    (ha : 0 < a) (ha1 : a ≤ 1) :
    (∀ q ∈ Set.Icc t 1, (∀ n y, 0 ≤ Real.exp (sprtS q₀ t y n)) ∧
      Supermartingale (fun n y => Real.exp (sprtS q₀ t y n)) pastFiltration
        (Measure.infinitePi fun _ : ℕ => bern q)) ∧
    (∀ q ∈ Set.Icc t 1,
      lawQ ν a q {ω | accepts (sprtRule W q₀ t δ) d ω} ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ) ∧
    (∀ q ∈ Set.Icc 0 q₀,
      lawQ ν a q {ω | stops (sprtRule W q₀ t δ) d ω ∧ ¬ accepts (sprtRule W q₀ t δ) d ω}
        ≤ ENNReal.ofReal δ) := by sorry

end PhysReaudit
